From: AutoBleem <autobleem@retromenele.pl>
Subject: [PATCH] input_keymaps: the PlayStation Classic's front buttons as RetroArch keys

The console's front buttons are keyboard keys: POWER is KEY_SLEEP (SDL: SDL_SCANCODE_SLEEP), RESET is
KEY_PLAYPAUSE ("play" in RetroArch's key names), OPEN is KEY_EJECTCD. RetroArch maps only KEY_POWER to
RETROK_POWER and nothing to KEY_EJECTCD, so two of the three could not be bound on a stock build.
KEY_SLEEP / SDLK_SLEEP are RETROK_POWER ("power") now and KEY_EJECTCD / SDLK_EJECT are RETROK_LAUNCH_MEDIA
("media") - added at the end of each table, because the RetroArch-key -> platform-key lookup the hotkeys
use is built by walking the table and the last entry for a RetroArch key wins (KEY_MEDIA / SDLK_MEDIASELECT
already claim "media"; placed earlier, the console's entries were overridden). AutoBleem's cfg binds RESET as input_exit_emulator ("play" - quits RetroArch, the launcher takes
over) and OPEN as input_menu_toggle ("media" - RetroArch's menu over the game); POWER stays the console's.
---
diff --git a/input/input_keymaps.c b/input/input_keymaps.c
index 972acc2..8b8444c 100644
--- a/input/input_keymaps.c
+++ b/input/input_keymaps.c
@@ -817,6 +817,11 @@ const struct rarch_key_map rarch_key_map_sdl[] = {
    { SDLK_AC_BOOKMARKS, RETROK_BROWSER_FAVORITES },
    { SDLK_VOLUMEUP,     RETROK_VOLUME_UP },
    { SDLK_VOLUMEDOWN,   RETROK_VOLUME_DOWN },
+   /* The PlayStation Classic's front buttons: POWER is SDLK_SLEEP, OPEN is SDLK_EJECT - as the
+    * "power" and "media" key names. Last on purpose: the RetroArch-key -> platform-key lookup the
+    * hotkeys use is built by walking this table, and the last entry for a RetroArch key wins. */
+   { SDLK_SLEEP,        RETROK_POWER },
+   { SDLK_EJECT,        RETROK_LAUNCH_MEDIA },
 #endif
 
    { 0, RETROK_UNKNOWN },
@@ -1384,6 +1389,11 @@ const struct rarch_key_map rarch_key_map_linux[] = {
    { KEY_SEARCH,       RETROK_BROWSER_SEARCH },
    { KEY_MEDIA,        RETROK_LAUNCH_MEDIA },
 #endif
+   /* The PlayStation Classic's front buttons: POWER is KEY_SLEEP, OPEN is KEY_EJECTCD - as the "power"
+    * and "media" key names. Last on purpose: the RetroArch-key -> platform-key lookup the hotkeys use
+    * is built by walking this table, and the last entry for a RetroArch key wins. */
+   { KEY_SLEEP,        RETROK_POWER },
+   { KEY_EJECTCD,      RETROK_LAUNCH_MEDIA },
 
    { 0, RETROK_UNKNOWN },
 };
